.TH RAMSTEIN 1 "2026-07-28" "ramstein 0.11.0" "ramstein manual"
.SH NAME
ramstein \- verb CLI for the ramstein memory daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ramstein
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ramstein
talks to
.BR ramsteind (8)
over its control socket and prints the answer. With no verb, it runs
.BR status .
Every verb accepts
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B status
Available memory, PSI pressure, burn rate, and ETA-to-OOM.
.TP
.B top " [\-\-swap] [\-\-limit N]"
Live per-process RSS, ranked (or swap-ranked with
.BR \-\-swap ).
.I N
defaults to 20, clamped 1\(en1000.
.TP
.B blame " [\-\-since T] [\-\-limit N]"
What grew in RSS since
.IR T ,
a join of two index samples: grown, new (absent from the base sample), or
gone (absent from the latest \(em shown as freed, negative).
.I T
is
.IR Ns / Nm / Nh / Nd
or
.IR YYYY-MM-DD ;
defaults to
.IR 10m .
.TP
.B swap " [\-\-limit N]"
Who's parked in swap, VmSwap descending.
.TP
.B zombies
Defunct processes and the parent not reaping them. Reads live
.IR /proc ,
not the index \(em zombies are a now-question.
.TP
.B oom
Risk snapshot (available/PSI/burn/ETA) plus the top 5 kill candidates by
the kernel's own
.IR /proc/<pid>/oom_score .
Read-only.
.TP
.B advise
One-line nudges: sustained pressure, a fast RSS grower, swap over half
full, unreaped zombies, another OOM-fighter active (naming which half of
.BR systemd-oomd (8)'s
swap/pressure enrollment is real when they disagree, e.g. "systemd-oomd
(pressure only, not swap)" \(em pressure-only coverage protects none of
the scenario
.B ramstein
exists for), ETA under an hour, shared memory (tmpfs/dev/shm) over
.IR advise_shmem_pct .
.TP
.BI calm " target " "[\-\-high SIZE|\-\-release|\-\-nice N|\-\-kill]"
The gentle levers, and the one ungentle one.
.I target
is a pid or an exact comm name \(em an ambiguous comm (more than one
matching process, routinely true for chrome/postgres/python) refuses with
the candidate list; pass a pid instead.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-high " SIZE"
Write the target's cgroup
.I memory.high
to
.I SIZE
(e.g.
.IR 500M ", " 2G ).
Clamped to
.RI [ 64M ", " MemTotal ]
and to at least 1.1x the target's current RSS \(em a size can never be
set low enough to instant-thrash-OOM the process it's meant to calm.
.TP
.B \-\-release
Clear
.I memory.high
back to
.IR max .
.TP
.BI \-\-nice " N"
Renice the target,
.I N
clamped 0\(en19 \(em
.B calm
only ever lowers priority, never raises it.
.TP
.B \-\-kill
SIGTERM, then an optional SIGKILL if the process is still alive 5 seconds
later. Requires a fresh interactive confirmation typed at a real TTY \(em
.B ramstein
prints the target's pid and comm and asks you to type the pid back. No
.BR \-\-yes ,
no environment override, no non-interactive path: a script piping
.B \-\-kill
is refused outright, every time, on purpose.
.RE
.TP
.BI autocalm " status|arm|dry|run"
Arms
.B calm
to act on its own, on a timer \(em never kill. Three independent gates,
all required before it acts for real: config
.RI ( auto_calm_enabled ,
off by default), the runtime armed state below (config\-persisted \(em
survives a daemon restart once armed, disarm any time with
.BR "autocalm dry" ),
and the
.B ramstein\-autocalm.timer
unit being manually enabled
.RI ( systemctl " " enable " " \-\-now ).
.RS
.TP
.B status
Current enabled/armed state, policy thresholds, and the last cycle's
outcome.
.TP
.B arm
Lets the next triggered cycle act for real (renice and/or a cgroup
.I memory.high
squeeze on the top RSS grower). Requires a real TTY and typing
.B arm
to confirm \(em lighter than
.BR \-\-kill 's
gate since every autocalm step is reversible, but never a bare flag.
Persists across daemon restarts once confirmed; consent does not expire
on its own.
.TP
.B dry
Back to disarmed \(em cycles keep computing and notifying, never acting.
Also persists across restarts.
.TP
.B run
Runs one check-and-maybe-act cycle immediately (what
.B ramstein\-autocalm.timer
calls periodically once enabled). Useful on demand to see what a cycle
would do.
.RE
.TP
.BI oomd " status|enroll|disenroll"
Enrolls this session into
.BR systemd-oomd (8)'s
swap\-kill protection. Ubuntu ships
.B systemd-oomd
configured to act on memory
.I pressure
for your session but never on sustained
.I swap
exhaustion \(em the scenario
.B ramstein
exists for has zero stock coverage until this is run. Writes a drop\-in
.RI ( ManagedOOMSwap=kill ),
never a hand edit; undone the same way it was done.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Whether systemd\-oomd is actually watching this session right now, not
merely configured to.
.TP
.B enroll
Writes the drop\-in, restarts
.B systemd-oomd
(required for it to notice \(em proven necessary, a config reload alone
does not trigger re\-discovery of already\-running units), then
re\-measures before ever reporting success. Requires a real TTY and
typing
.B enroll
to confirm. Refuses outright, naming the remedy, if memory
.I and
swap are already both past systemd\-oomd's own trigger threshold \(em
enrolling in that moment would hand process selection to a kill with no
grace period, when
.B ramstein oom
can show the same candidates for you to choose from instead. This
refusal is a compiled\-in invariant; it will rarely fire on a healthy
machine, which is correct.
.TP
.B disenroll
Removes the drop\-in, restarts
.B systemd-oomd,
and confirms the machine is back to its default (unenrolled unless
something else independently enrolled it).
.RE
.TP
.BI swappiness " status|set N|reset"
.IR vm.swappiness ,
persisted and applied live \(em no service to restart. Writes a
.BR sysctl.d (5)
drop\-in
.RI ( /etc/sysctl.d/90\-ramstein\-swappiness.conf )
for reboot survival and the live kernel value in the same call.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Current live value, whether RAMstein's drop\-in is present, and the
ledgered pre\-RAMstein value if one has been set.
.TP
.BI set " N"
.I N
is 0\(en200. Requires a real TTY and typing
.B set
to confirm. Ledgers the value from
.I before
RAMstein's first change \(em never overwritten by a later
.BR set ,
so
.B reset
always restores the true original. Re\-measures
.I /proc/sys/vm/swappiness
before reporting success; a drop\-in written without the live value
moving is a failure, not a partial success.
.TP
.B reset
Restores the ledgered pre\-RAMstein value and removes the drop\-in.
Errors cleanly if RAMstein has never changed
.I vm.swappiness
on this machine.
.RE
.TP
.BI swap\-size " status|set SIZE|remove"
A standalone, additive swap file \(em its own backing file
.RI ( /var/lib/ramstein/extra.img )
and its own standalone
.BR systemd.swap (5)
unit, never touching the machine's own existing swap or
.IR /etc/fstab .
Genuinely BOUNDED\-WAIT: creating or resizing the file
.RI ( fallocate " + " mkswap )
scales with size.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Active size, disk headroom, and the last change's outcome
.RI ( pending
while one is running).
.TP
.BI set " SIZE"
.I SIZE
is e.g.
.IR 4G " or " 16G .
Requires a real TTY and typing
.B set
to confirm. Reports
.I pending
immediately \(em the daemon runs the real work on a background thread \(em
and the CLI polls
.B status
for the real outcome rather than blocking the socket. Refuses up front
if the resize would leave less than
.I swap_size_min_disk_headroom_gb
free on the backing filesystem: an oversized swap file trading a RAM
crisis for a disk crisis is exactly the mistake this blocks. Re\-measures
via
.B swapon \-\-show
before ever reporting success.
.TP
.B remove
Turns the swap off and deletes the backing file. Errors cleanly if
RAMstein has no managed swap file on this machine.
.RE
.TP
.BI zram " status|enable|disable"
Compressed RAM\-backed swap via
.BR systemd\-zram\-generator (8).
Writes
.I /etc/systemd/zram\-generator.conf
directly rather than a drop\-in \(em self\-contained, inert with no
.I [zram0]
section, none of an
.I /etc/fstab
edit's risk. Genuinely BOUNDED\-WAIT, same shape as
.BR swap\-size .
Needs the
.B systemd\-zram\-generator
package (a RAMstein dependency).
.RS
.TP
.B status
Whether the generator package is installed, whether RAMstein's config
section is present, active size, and the last change's outcome
.RI ( pending
while one is running).
.TP
.B enable
Requires a real TTY and typing
.B enable
to confirm. Writes the config section, reloads (re\-running the
generator), and starts
.IR systemd\-zram\-setup@zram0.service .
Re\-measures via
.B swapon \-\-show
before ever reporting success.
.TP
.B disable
Removes the config section and stops the device. No confirmation
required \(em undoing a RAMstein\-made change.
.RE
.TP
.BI update " [\-\-check] [\-\-json]"
Delegates straight to
.BR ramstein\-update (1)
(the family's shared update spine \(em Wave B). With no arguments,
the manual-install consent tier; with
.BR \-\-check ,
report-only (what the pill's own update row polls, no root needed).
Never runs unattended: the daily
.B ramstein\-update.timer
only ever passes
.BR \-\-check .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ ramstein status
ramstein v0.5.0   (status 0s old)
 ! mem 45.2G available of 61.2G   swap 5.1G free of 8.0G   pressure some 0.0/full 0.0   burn 9.8M/s   OOM ~87m

$ ramstein top \-\-limit 3
top by rss   (sample 10s ago)
     RSS     SWAP       PID  PROC
  671.7M       0B    515128    claude
  645.5M       0B   2311838    python3
  640.9M       0B   1552474    claude

$ ramstein blame \-\-since 5m \-\-limit 3
RSS movers over the last 5m:
  +  645.5M  python3          pid 2311838 (now 645.5M) new
  +  329.2M  chrome\-headless  pid 2312307 (now 329.2M) new
  +  230.0M  nautilus         pid 2291973 (now 230.0M) new

$ ramstein oom
available 45.2G of 61.2G   pressure some 0.0/full 0.0   burn 9.8M/s   OOM ~87m
who dies first (by oom_score):
    870    390.0M   2312307  chrome\-headless
    869    294.8M   2274175  chrome

$ ramstein advise
\- 2 zombie(s) unreaped \(em warp\-terminal isn't reaping (2 of them)
\- systemd\-oomd is active \(em RAMstein's kill prompts stay advisory\-only, standing down

$ ramstein calm 2312307 \-\-nice 10
! systemd\-oomd is active \(em proceeding, but it may already be handling this
chrome\-headless (pid 2312307): nice \-> 10

$ ramstein autocalm status
auto\-calm: enabled=False  armed=False
  trigger: PSI some > 20.0% or full > 10.0% or swap storm
  steps: renice+squeeze  (nice=15, squeeze to 130% rss, cooldown 300s)
  no cycles run yet
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/ramstein/status.json
The read seam \(em memory, swap, pressure, burn, ETA, and the M2/M3 pill
digest. Mode 0640.
.TP
.I /run/ramstein/control.sock
The command socket. Mode 0660, peercred-gated.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RAMSTEIN_RUNTIME_DIR
Overrides
.I /run/ramstein
(status.json and control.sock live here). Used for testing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero if the daemon is unreachable, or if the daemon answers with an
error (bad arguments, ambiguous target, refused kill, etc.) \(em the
message explains why.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ramsteind (8),
.BR ramstein\-healthcheck (1),
.BR ramstein\-update (1)
.SH AUTHOR
asuramaya and RAMstein contributors.
